  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## go-streams \u00b7 Runner & Saturation Deep Dive\n**Question this dashboard answers:** *Is the application keeping up \u2014 and if not, where is pressure building: input (lag), workers (queues/backpressure), poll loop, or sink (produce)?*\n\nThe **Backpressure** row only has data for the `PartitionedRunner`; the `SingleThreadedRunner` processes inline and has no queues. When a partition's worker channel fills, go-streams pauses that partition at the consumer \u2014 rising *paused depth* is the earliest backpressure signal.\n\nReading order: lag tells you *whether* you're behind; queue/paused depth tells you the workers are the bottleneck; poll panels rule the broker fetch path in or out; produce panels rule the sink out. Use the Topology Explorer to find *which node* makes workers slow."
      },
      "transparent": true
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Input saturation \u00b7 consumer lag",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Consumer lag percentiles",
      "description": "p50 / p95 / p99 record age at consume time (stream.consumer.lag) across selected topics. Docs suggest alerting when p99 exceeds 30 s.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(stream_consumer_lag_bucket{job=~\"$job\", messaging_destination_name=~\"$topic\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(stream_consumer_lag_bucket{job=~\"$job\", messaging_destination_name=~\"$topic\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(stream_consumer_lag_bucket{job=~\"$job\", messaging_destination_name=~\"$topic\"}[$__rate_interval])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s",
          "min": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineWidth": 1,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "pointSize": 4,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "gradientMode": "none",
            "thresholdsStyle": {
              "mode": "off"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "heatmap",
      "title": "Consumer lag distribution",
      "description": "Heatmap of stream.consumer.lag. A drifting band means falling steadily behind; a split band means specific partitions are lagging \u2014 check the per-partition panel.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (le) (rate(stream_consumer_lag_bucket{job=~\"$job\", messaging_destination_name=~\"$topic\"}[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{le}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "format": "heatmap"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "calculate": false,
        "cellGap": 1,
        "color": {
          "mode": "scheme",
          "scheme": "Spectral",
          "steps": 64,
          "reverse": false,
          "exponent": 0.5,
          "fill": "dark-orange"
        },
        "yAxis": {
          "unit": "s",
          "axisPlacement": "left"
        },
        "legend": {
          "show": true
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "single",
          "showColorScale": true
        },
        "exemplars": {
          "color": "rgba(255,0,255,0.7)"
        },
        "filterValues": {
          "le": 1e-09
        },
        "rowsFrame": {
          "layout": "auto"
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Lag p99 by partition (top 10)",
      "description": "Worst partitions by p99 lag (stream.consumer.lag by partition id). One hot partition usually means key skew; all partitions lagging means general under-capacity.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
